course: dictionary
lesson: 13077
title: Fictional: made up or real?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fictional means invented, made up, and not real. A writer or storyteller creates a fictional thing from their imagination. «The dragon in the story is fictional.» No dragon lives in real life, so the story is made up.
explain: Fiction is the noun. It means stories that are imagined rather than true. Fictional is the adjective that describes them. «The fictional town in the book has a talking clock.» The town is not on any real map, but the writer makes the reader picture it.
explain: Fictional things can still feel real and be loved by readers. «Paddington Bear is a fictional character, but many children feel he is their friend.» Being fictional does not make a character less exciting. It only means the character was invented.
fact: Fictional means invented, made up, or not real.
fact: Fiction means stories that are imagined rather than true.
fact: «Harry Potter» and «Paddington Bear» are fictional characters.
fact: A fictional TV show is not the news, because the news reports real events.
exercise: «The dragon in the story is fictional.» What does fictional mean? | True, as shown on the news | Found in a museum | Very large and scaly | *Made up and not real
exercise: Mia sorts her books into fiction and non-fiction. Which book belongs in fiction? | A book about how volcanoes form | A guide to growing carrots | A list of the planets and their sizes | *A story about a talking fox who goes to school
exercise: «Paddington Bear is a fictional character.» Find and copy the word that means made up. | character | Paddington | *fictional | Bear
test: Which of these is a fictional character? | The head teacher of your school | The weather presenter on the news | A real queen who lived in 1800 | *Paddington Bear
test: Jay says the news is fictional. Why is he wrong? | The news is a story about dragons | The news is always funny | *The news reports real events, so it is not made up | The news has a presenter, so it must be made up
exam: Which word best means made up and not real? | Factual | Honest | Historical | *Fictional
